26-09-18","committee":"18 September 2026","paper_title":"Update on Pension Fund Activity: Quarterly Investment Update Report","paper_url":"https://cmis.essex.gov.uk/Essexcmis5/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=e5TxNlXtfLYMu1aZqdhNT4kj8tvgj0dCuBVIbGtVhj7kp5m7ZkHYxw%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"All eight strategic investment risks remain above their target scores","detail":"As of 31 August 2026, none of the eight Strategic Investment Risks identified in the fund's risk register are currently at their target levels; all remain elevated. No new risks were identified and mitigation actions continue to be reviewed, but the persistent elevation of the entire risk portfolio above targets indicates ongoing investment governance concerns.","category":"governance","matters":"Pension fund investment risk reflects on the council's financial governance and asset stewardship; sustained elevation of all strategic risks above target suggests systematic investment challenges that could impair the fund's returns or resilience.","figures":"8 Strategic Investment Risks; all above target; 0 new risks identified","quote":"all eight Strategic Investment Risks remained above their target scores, with no changes recorded","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"17 September 2026","paper_title":"Essex Highways Performance - Year 14","paper_url":"https://cmis.essex.gov.uk/Essexcmis5/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=78PzodjOzvqhFepHRQ%2fWYaYTz3CNy0LVISFmfgMqiDstOlUR6PEFjA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Local road defect backlog stands at 16,994 outstanding repairs, more than triple the <5000 target","detail":"Outstanding defects on local roads have increased from 15,600 in April 2025 to 16,994 by March 2026. This metric has exceeded its 5000-defect target in every single month reported. The steady climbing trend, with no month showing improvement towards target, indicates sustained pressure on the council's maintenance capacity.","category":"capital","matters":"An oversized defect backlog across the local road network represents deferred maintenance that will eventually require costlier remediation and signals the council may lack sufficient capital resources or operational efficiency to maintain its asset base, a factor lenders consider when assessing creditworthiness.","figures":"April 2025: 15,600 defects; March 2026: 16,994 defects; Target: <5000","quote":"Number of outstanding defects on Local road network <5000 ... 15,600 15,829 15,657 15,833 15,485 15,316 15,544 15,574 15,849 16,088 16,564 16,994 16,994","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"17 September 2026","paper_title":"Essex Highways Performance - Year 14","paper_url":"https://cmis.essex.gov.uk/Essexcmis5/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=78PzodjOzvqhFepHRQ%2fWYaYTz3CNy0LVISFmfgMqiDstOlUR6PEFjA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Outstanding defects on principal roads (PR1/PR2) have grown 51% to 11,602, far exceeding the <1000 target","detail":"The number of defects outstanding on the council's principal road network has climbed steadily from 7,689 in April 2025 to 11,602 by March 2026, tracking consistently well above the stated threshold of <1000. The trend shows no month achieved the target. This represents a sustained and growing maintenance backlog on the network classified as most important.","category":"capital","matters":"A large and growing defect backlog on principal roads signals either underfunding of maintenance or operational failure to keep pace with demand. Lenders assess this as an unfunded infrastructure liability that reduces a council's financial resilience and may constrain future borrowing capacity.","figures":"April 2025: 7,689 defects; March 2026: 11,602 defects; Target: <1000","quote":"Number of outstanding defects on PR1 and PR2 network <1000 ... 7,689 7,747 7,943 7,916 7,816 8,026 8,164 8,419 8,904 9,509 10,420 11,602 11,602","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"16 September 2026","paper_title":"Adoption of All-Ages Carers Strategy 2026 and Procurement of single lead provider for Unpaid Carers Services (FP/047/03/26)","paper_url":"https://cmis.essex.gov.uk/Essexcmis5/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=3ttCJXC0zO4puTmaM%2bmLa%2f0Ql2FAWpnpNA%2f6nbbS9XaFhkZMASqNGw%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Financial model assumes a \u00a368k annual saving from reduced Carers Direct Payments, but demand has been growing","detail":"The budget model projects a small saving of \u00a368k annually by assuming the new service model will reduce demand for formal Adult Social Care assessments. However, Carers Direct Payments (CDPs) have \"continued to grow\" and reached \u00a32.7m in 2025/26. The paper acknowledges explicitly that \"the risk of that not materialising will need to be monitored\", suggesting the council is uncertain the assumed efficiency gain will occur.","category":"demand","matters":"The funding model is already tight (using reserves in year one, BCF at risk); if CDP demand does not fall as projected, the gap would need to be met from other budgets or further reserve draw, squeezing other Adult Social Care provision.","figures":"CDPs reached \u00a32.7m in 2025/26; \u00a368k assumed annual saving; current GDP trend is upward not downward","quote":"This funding model relies on a small decline in that spend (see 6.2.7 below) and so the risk of that not materialising will need to be monitored.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"16 September 2026","paper_title":"Adoption of All-Ages Carers Strategy 2026 and Procurement of single lead provider for Unpaid Carers Services (FP/047/03/26)","paper_url":"https://cmis.essex.gov.uk/Essexcmis5/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=3ttCJXC0zO4puTmaM%2bmLa%2f0Ql2FAWpnpNA%2f6nbbS9XaFhkZMASqNGw%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Better Care Fund (BCF) future funding is flagged as at material risk","detail":"The paper explicitly flags that BCF funding (which covers 77% of total three-year cost from year 2 onwards) may reduce or have conditions changed \"as part of reforms\". The council notes this risk will \"need to be managed by partners within the overall pooled budget\", but offers no fallback if BCF reduces materially.","category":"income","matters":"BCF is the primary funding source for years 2-3 of the new contract. A reduction would force either service cuts or use of additional reserves, and the council has little control over this decision as it is held jointly with NHS Essex ICB.","figures":"Better Care Fund funds \u00a3353k in year 1, \u00a31.94m in year 2, \u00a31.97m in year 3 = \u00a34.26m of the \u00a35.82m total cost","quote":"There is a risk that the funding available through the BCF will reduce, or conditions change in future years as part of reforms.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-18"},"name":"Essex CC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"All eight strategic investment risks remain above their target scores","lead":"Pension fund investment risk reflects on the council's financial governance and asset stewardship; sustained elevation of all strategic risks above target suggests systematic investment challenges that could impair the fund's returns or resilience.","also":["16 other findings in this window"],"watch":null,"n_findings":17,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Update on Pension Fund Activity: Quarterly Investment Update Report","top_paper_url":"https://cmis.essex.gov.uk/Essexcmis5/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=e5TxNlXtfLYMu1aZqdhNT4kj8tvgj0dCuBVIbGtVhj7kp5m7ZkHYxw%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","draft":true},"findings_total":79,"news_drafts_total":3}}